The bridge-free definition rebuilds but the symbolic three-plus proof gets stuck. More importantly, the body-sensitivity test gives a concrete false-conclusion witness: after changing only the recursive base result to `"a"`, real Python and fresh `krun` execution return `"a"` for `"bbb"`, yet the bridge-enabled K theory still proves `#Top` for the false claim that it returns `""`. I’m now running the separate required false-postcondition mutation against the unmodified candidate.
